      "title": "Aggregate row counts do not prove the prepared-plan slot bijection",
      "locations": [
        "overlay/src/cryptanalysis/ecbench/retained_attempt_join.rs:84-117",
        "overlay/src/cryptanalysis/ecbench/retained_attempt_join.rs:211-292"
      ],
      "evidence": "The validator accepts seven caller-supplied hex digests and counts primary/measured rows and arm-seed triplets. It does not read plan files, represent plan sequence/round/role, require 1260 workload identities or 18 slots per workload, compare complete identity across a pair, or bind retries to primaries.",
      "impact": "Fabricated schedules, cross-workload/cross-plan pairs, and arbitrary retry rows can pass the advertised 22680/18900/6300 geometry.",
      "required_correction": "Parse hash-bound prepared plans, recompute all slots, join every primary and retry to those slots, and compare the complete scheduled identity."
